\name{cellucid_history_tracker_start}
\alias{cellucid_history_tracker_start}
\title{Start another tracker}
\usage{
cellucid_history_tracker_start(viewer, name, start = "opened")
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{name}{A name, unique among its kind (compared without case and extra spaces); no length limit. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{start}{opened: the dataset as it was opened; shown: what is shown now. One of \code{"opened"}, \code{"shown"}. Default \code{"opened"}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{head} (The step shown now), \code{tracker}.
}
\description{
Start a new tracker, an independent tree of steps on this dataset: from the dataset as opened (the default), or from what is shown.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.tracker.start} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_tracker_start(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
